    "difficulty": 1,
    "stem": "Which command creates a new local branch **and** switches to it in Git 2.23+?",
    "options": [
      { "id": "A", "text": "`git branch new-feature`" },
      { "id": "B", "text": "`git switch -c new-feature`" },
      { "id": "C", "text": "`git checkout new-feature`" },
      { "id": "D", "text": "`git reset --hard new-feature`" }
    ],
    "correctAnswers": ["B"],
    "explanation": "`git switch -c` is the modern, purpose-built command; the older `git checkout -b` still works but is discouraged for new material.",
    "optionExplanations": {
      "A": "Creates the branch without switching.",
      "B": "Correct — combines create + switch.",
      "C": "Without `-b` this only switches to an existing branch.",
      "D": "`reset` rewrites history and does not create branches."
    },
